## 3. System Architecture & Data Flow

This flowchart describes the frontend structure of the React app and how the data is processed, analyzed, and persisted.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Client [React Frontend App]
        UI[App.jsx / User Interface]
        Lang[translations.js - English & Kannada translations]
        Chat[chatbotEngine.js - Chatbot Q&A System]
        RecEng[recommendationEngine.js - Fertilizer Matching Rules]
    end

    subgraph Backend [Supabase Backend]
        SupaClient[supabaseClient.js - API Communication]
        Auth[Row-Level Security / RLS policies]
        DB[(PostgreSQL Database)]
    end

    %% Client Interactions
    UI -->|1. Enters soil metrics & crop choice| RecEng
    UI -->|Ask questions| Chat
    Chat -->|Return dynamic chatbot replies| UI

    %% Algorithm Flow
    RecEng -->|2. Computes recommendations & matches| UI
    RecEng -->|3. Resolves Fertilizer specs| SupaClient

    %% Database Writes
    UI -->|4. Transmits farmer, soil report, and result| SupaClient
    SupaClient -->|5. Performs CRUD inserts/queries| Auth
    Auth -->|6. Stores records safely| DB

    %% Database Tables mapping
    subgraph SQL_Tables [DB Tables in supabase_setup.sql]
        tbl_farmers[(farmers)]
        tbl_soil_reports[(soil_reports)]
        tbl_recommendations[(recommendations)]
        tbl_fertilizers[(fertilizers)]
    end

    DB --- tbl_farmers
    DB --- tbl_soil_reports
    DB --- tbl_recommendations
    DB --- tbl_fertilizers
```

